course: dictionary
lesson: 7558
title: Teeth words: premolar
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A premolar is a tooth at the side of your mouth. It sits between the pointed canine teeth and the big flat molars at the back. Its name tells you where it is: pre means before, so it comes before the molars.
explain: Premolars have two points, and they help crush food. In a science lesson you learn that incisors cut, canines tear, and premolars and molars crush and grind. «A grown-up set has 8 incisors for cutting, 4 canines for gripping, 8 premolars and 12 molars for grinding.» Each kind of tooth has its own job.
explain: Premolar can also be an adjective, meaning to do with these teeth. You might read about «upper premolar» or «lower premolar», which tells you which jaw the tooth is in. When you see a new word, ask: is it a thing, or does it describe a thing?
fact: A premolar is one of the teeth between the canines and the molars.
fact: Premolars have two points and help crush food.
fact: «Premolars and molars» are the teeth we use for crushing and grinding.
fact: Adults have eight premolars.
fact: Children's milk teeth have no premolars.
exercise: «A grown-up set has 8 incisors for cutting, 4 canines for gripping, 8 premolars and 12 molars for grinding.» What do premolars help you do? | Make a whistling sound | Tear meat | *Crush food | Cut food into thin strips
exercise: «A grown-up set has 8 incisors for cutting, 4 canines for gripping, 8 premolars and 12 molars for grinding.» How many premolars does a grown-up have? | 12 | 4 | 20 | *8
exercise: Premolars sit between which two kinds of teeth? | *Canines and molars | Two molars | Milk teeth and incisors | Canines and incisors
test: In science, premolars and molars are used for what job? | Whistling | *Crushing and grinding | Cutting | Tearing
test: Do children's milk teeth have premolars? | *No | Yes, eight of them | Yes, four of them | Only the top ones
exam: Which meaning fits premolar as an adjective, as in «upper premolar»? | Before the teeth, at the front of the mouth | *To do with premolar teeth | Very large or heavy | A kind of sweet or treat
